Parent companion for FPGA-gPTP #82 (merged; reset publication) in the milan_dp
suite. The five changed expectations below (three in sim_gptp.cpp, two in
sim_ax1x1gptp.cpp) fail at gptp-processor 43acfbcc (the base
of #84/#85), before this lane's change, and at every later head: they assert
the pre-#82 boot state (grandmaster 0). It rides the same gptp-processor pin
adoption. Apply after parent-adoption-milan_dp-85.patch (it uses that patch's
THIS_CLOCK / kThisClock constants):
git apply parent-adoption-milan_dp-82.patch

Before any peer, a PTP Instance with no port priority vector is its own
grandmaster and its pathTrace is {thisClock} (IEEE 802.1AS-2020 10.3.13.2.4
b) and i)). That first real grandmaster identity is a change, so the parent's
clock validity arms its Milan v1.2 Annex B.1.1 holdover
(KL_ptp_clock_validity: "the active owner's first publication of a real
grandmaster id IS a change and arms the holdover").

tb/verilator/milan_dp/sim_gptp.cpp (legs gptp and gptp-lat):

| Line | Expectation | Was | Now |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| 817-819 | comment: the committed bank is zero before any peer | zero | thisClock is grandmaster; parent and pdelay zero; holdover armed |
| 825 | fabric GM low overrides SW | 0 | low word of THIS_CLOCK |
| 826 | fabric GM high overrides SW | 0 | high word of THIS_CLOCK |
| new | reset publication of thisClock arms the holdover (CLKV_STAT bit 3) | - | 1 |
| 835 | compatibility CLKV fields read zero (bits 2..15, now except bit 3, the holdover) | mask 0x3FFF | mask 0x3FFD |

tb/verilator/milan_dp/sim_ax1x1gptp.cpp (physical-rate leg, tb/verilator/milan_dp_gptp):

| Line | Expectation | Was | Now |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| 1149 | pre-acquisition GET_AVB_INFO grandmaster | 0 ("has no selected GM") | kThisClock ("names thisClock as GM") |
| 1197 | public GM right after a reset | 0 ("reset clears complete public GM") | kThisClock ("reset publishes thisClock as GM") |

